    category: "bioinformatics",
    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-10-30, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (115 hits across 27 queries, scan regenerated 2026-10-30 06:0x KST via 'bash run.sh scan', 0 source errors). The score-9 top band was again entirely RECYCLED against the retained id:136-id:140 window (GSE328275 TNBC-CD45 immune atlas, GSE328422 sequential lymph-node metastasis spatial, GSE326553 Oprm1-A118G opioid CosMx, GSE281463/64/65 chromatin-GWAS bundle), so the actionable harvest comes from the score-7 and score-6 ladder after accession-level dedupe against the page-level GSE retention set (33 accessions retained on the page; the three picks below are all accession-level NOVEL, verified against their NCBI GEO esummary records for title, depositor abstract, taxon, pdat, sample count and supplementary-file availability rather than title-matching alone). Signal 1 is GSE341532 (Mus musculus, n=12, pdat 2026/10/05, SubSeries of GSE341533, NIA-IRP/NIH Computational Biology & Genomics Core): a lifespan- and sex-resolved single-cell multi-omic atlas of mouse liver integrating RNA and ATAC across five age groups, which resolves continuous non-linear regulatory dynamics that binary young-versus-old contrasts cannot infer, identifies cell-type-, zone-, age- and sex-resolved transcription factor regulation, oscillatory metabolic programs, distinct emerging senotypes and extensive chromatin plasticity, and surfaces a transient female-specific activation of the pro-neural pioneer factor Ascl1 that marks hepatocytes entering a regenerative-like cell cycle but is selectively lost in geriatric age. Signal 2 is GSE343647 (Homo sapiens, n=12, pdat 2026/10/28): a three-dimensional Matrigel-based droplet microfluidic screening platform that functionally isolates killer and non-killer NK cells before transcriptomic profiling, applied to donor-matched MSLN-CAR CIML NK cells and CIML controls from three independent donors, revealing widespread lncRNA downregulation in killer populations that is conserved across donors and more pronounced in the engineered CAR condition, with candidate lncRNA-gene pairs prioritised by genomic proximity and coordinated co-expression. Signal 3 is GSE352026 (Homo sapiens, n=21, pdat 2026/10/28): QUAIL-100, a quadruple-attenuated Listeria monocytogenes strain (Lm ΔactA/ΔinlB/ΔribC/ΔribF), evaluated in PBMCs from 7 healthy donors and 8 pediatric patients at day 30 after αβ-depleted haploidentical HSCT, showing that combinatorial phosphoantigen, PAM and co-stimulatory signalling avoids the rapid terminal differentiation and exhaustion that limit standard Vγ9Vδ2 activation with zoledronic acid, with longitudinal 10-day flow profiling plus day-7 scRNA-seq, AbSeq and V(D)J sequencing.",
